From 847887ec3c86ad4e028cc57e79e776954c060d40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:43:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Gate idle heartbeat/loop scans and cache board row
 materialization

Fifth idle-CPU cut, core half (kanban t_01a19d7fc2cfe36a, parent t_01a199a0a5d38255).

- gateway/run_idle_gates.py, run_goals.py, hermes_cli/loops.py: heartbeat
  restore and loop watcher cache only proven-empty metadata keyed on the same
  reader connection revision (data_version + total_changes); active, corrupt and
  error results are never cached. Root loop watch gates before listing; quiet
  parser option avoids per-sweep warnings for corrupt rows while still retrying.
- plugins/kanban/dashboard/board_rows.py (new), board_read.py (new),
  plugin_api.py, board_prewarm.py: split SQL row materialization from payload
  projection; retained board_rows observer registered with kanban_generation
  (WAL/SHM fencing) so recover/connect is never pinned. Whole-payload TTL
  unchanged; clock/config/profiles/replica/diagnostics projected each refresh.

Tests: tests/gateway/test_run_idle_gates_empty_proofs.py,
tests/plugins/test_kanban_board_rows_cache.py (new), board_read_cache updated.
414 pass (40 files) + 120 pass/8 skip generation/lockguard/recovery; 12/12
safeguard mutations caught. Native Mac copied-data replay: board refresh
-69.52% interval CPU, heartbeat+loop -89.16%, per-tick output hashes equal.
